tmas. I enjoyed getting a ride in a cable car.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, that was fun.<br>", "id": 2, "time": "12000", "image": "engenn5le04ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, and the Palace of Fine Arts was awesome. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Did you like the collection of modern art we saw?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Oh yeah, that exhibit was different, wasn't it!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could you explain what you mean?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: We saw some cool paintings, but modern art is not really for me.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  OK, I understand.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I didn't like the visit to the police station.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh yeah, just forget about that part.<br>", "id": 3, "time": "20000", "image": "engenn5le04ob11re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa in San Francisco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "You're Leaving Tomorrow!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le04ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about: <br><ul><li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly </li><li>a general truth</li><li>to give personal information </li> "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Simple Present. <br><br> You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>. <br><br> You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:  <ul><li>a current event or action happening around now  </li><li>events that <span class=\"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)  </li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now </span> or<span class=\"italic\"> later </span> with the Present Continuous. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I understand what you mean.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You're leaving tomorrow!</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What do you mean by that?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I am looking forward to coming back next year.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Review of Modals"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You often use a modal like <span class=\"italic\">can, may, could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to ask for permission.  <br><br>  You also use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may, might</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to show possibility. <br> <br>The modal <span class=\"italic\">could</span> is used to ask for clarification.<br><br>Modals are placed before a verb in the base form. The verb does not change."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Can I come back next year?  (permission)</span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You could come back this summer.  (possibility)</span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Could you explain what you mean (by that)?  (clarification) </span> "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "police station"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the place where police officers work "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm in a police station. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "decorated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "made to look better by adding things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: City Hall is decorated with flashing lights. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "marina"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area where privately owned boats such as yachts are kept "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We went shopping down at the marina."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cable car"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of bus used in San Francisco"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We got into an accident with a couple of cable cars"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ride"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "taking someone to a place, usually in a car"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A kind taxi driver offered me a ride."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "took "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the verb <span class=\"italic\">to take</span> in the Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I took a bus from the airport."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of a destination. It can be a place you went to or a place you want to go to."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue. Talk about what you did on the trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what you liked best."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about other things you enjoyed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you didn't like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your dialogue to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue of 8 - 10 lines about an experience on a trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what I liked the most."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what I enjoyed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what I didn't like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice the dialogue with a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}